=== Prompt ===
Who is Kratos from God of War?

=== Response ===
Kratos is the protagonist of the God of War series, a popular action-adventure game franchise developed by Santa Monica Studio and published by Sony Interactive Entertainment. Kratos is a Spartan warrior who is known for his incredible strength and rage.

In the first God of War game, Kratos is a vengeful anti-hero who seeks to overthrow the Olympian gods after they betray and punish him for a mistake in his past. As the series progresses, Kratos undergoes significant character development, becoming a more thoughtful and introspective character, especially in the 2018 reboot of the series.

In the 2018 God of War, Kratos is no longer the vengeful warrior he once was. He has moved on from his past and is trying to start a new life with his son Atreus in the Norse realms. Kratos is still a powerful warrior, but he is also a father and a mentor, trying to protect his son while also teaching him the ways of the world.

Kratos is voiced by actor Terrence C. Carson in the first three games of the series, and by Christopher Judge in the 2018 reboot and beyond. He is considered one of the most iconic video game characters of all time, and has a large and dedicated fan base.

